"<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"Gregory-Schwing-MD-PhD\"} -->\n_Requested by **greg** in the project symphony_5's thread \"Run morphometry on gold tier 3 masks\"_\n\nAdds the export PR 45's stage 1 reads: `python -m morphometry run --lines` writes the lines morphoview draws, each with its two named ends, and each measured vertebra's frame beside the rows, so the export can ride in the morphometry jobs. Nothing here reads a real mask or CT, and no grid job is queued; the owner held the jobs at 14:45 UTC on 30 October until a resynthesis.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- `run --lines` writes, per study, `lines/ID.csv` and `frames/ID.csv` beside `rows/ID.csv`, and joins them at the end as `lines.csv` and `frames.csv`.\n  - A line row holds study, level, key, part, rule, panel, value, measured, drawn and status, and its two ends (ax, ay, az, bx, by, bz) in world millimetres of the mask's affine, each named in `a_end` and `b_end` (`morphoview.lines.ENDS`: left or right, posterior or anterior, inferior or superior, medial or lateral, the canal or the tip). A disc's line is named in the frame of the vertebra below it.\n  - A vertebra has the lines of the 25 keys `morphoview.lines.VERTEBRA_KEYS` names, Panjabi's seven chords among them, and a disc those of its three heights (`DISC_KEYS`). The other keys, 56 of the 81 a lumbar vertebra's rows hold, have no line.\n  - A further segment a line carries (the wedge's lower plate, Eisenstein's apex-to-apex line) is a row of its own, named in `part`, with no value.\n  - A frame row is the vertebra's origin (its label's main piece's centroid) and its three axes, which axis z lies along (`axis`: bisector, one plate or column line) and the column's line z was turned from (cx, cy, cz).\n  - Ends, values and frames are written whole, to the bit; `measured` is the row's value to four places.\n- `morphoview.lines` draws Panjabi's posterior height at the wall and the canal's width and depth at the pedicles (`panjabi_height`, `panjabi_canal`), which had no line. Each is a median, drawn in the cell or section nearest it.\n- The lines are built by `morphoview.lines` on the vertebrae `measure_volume` built (its new `keep`) and checked against the values it wrote, so a line never shows a measure other than the row's. Each line says drawn, withheld or not measured. Each builder has its own guard: one that fails gets a `flag:lines` row naming it and loses only its own lines.\n- The lines and frames are written before the rows, and the rows stay the commit marker. A run with the lines has a stamp of its own, over `morphoview/lines.py` too, so a study measured without them is measured again, as is one whose lines or frames file is missing. The joins take only the studies whose rows carry the run's stamp, and are written to a part file and moved into place.\n- `morphoview.lines.pedicles` takes the measure's own reading of each side (`side_reading`), since reading `pedicle.one_side` again took five sixths of a study's drawing on the phantoms (3.5 of 4.2 s of CPU on L2 to L4 at 0.8 by 0.8 by 1 mm); on a vertebra the volume's edge cuts, whose values the measure blanks, it reads the side again. On three phantom columns, one worker, the drawing adds 9 per cent to the measuring of L1 to L5 and 13 to that of C2 to C7 and of C2 to L5, and nothing to the peak memory.\n\n## How it was checked\n\n- `morphometry/tests/test_lines_export.py`, 25 tests on phantoms of L2 to L4 (straight at 0.8 by 0.8 by 1 mm; the same cut through L4's body by the volume's edge; the same on 2.5 mm slices; and a chain whose joints open 8 degrees, tilt 4, turn 5 and slip 4 mm):\n  - every line of the whole column is drawn and holds its row's value, and every one of the seven chords is drawn at each level;\n  - the keys drawn are the ones `VERTEBRA_KEYS` and `DISC_KEYS` name, and every end is named;\n  - every length's ends lie its value apart, to the bit, and every frame is orthonormal and right-handed to the bit;\n  - on the chain, the origin is the main piece's centroid, each line's ends share in its frame what its builder gave them (a height's local x, a width's local y and z), y points to the body, z up and x to the right, each end lies where its name says, and each frame names its axis and lies off the column's line;\n  - a cut body's lines all say not measured, and the level above it is drawn whole;\n  - resumption: a missing lines or frames file brings its study back, a study killed at any of its three writes is measured again, and the stamps differ with and without the lines;\n  - a builder that fails flags its level and loses only its own lines; a study that fails, before or after its vertebrae are kept, writes empty lines and frames and is measured again;\n  - a run a dead worker cut short joins only the studies of its own stamp and leaves no part file;\n  - the reused pedicle reading draws what reading again draws, on an uncut L3 and on the cut L4.\n- Each test the fixes added fails with its fix taken out: 28 mutants, all caught. The first round's one survivor, the canal's depth read on the wrong section, led to the test that holds each median's line to its cell or section; the first round's 13 were run again on the final tree, and the two of the second round that move an end's name were run again once the end-name test read every pair either way round.\n- The engine's suite: `python -m unittest morphometry.tests.test_morphometry morphometry.tests.test_lines_export morphoview.tests.test_lines` gives 75 tests, all passing (test_morphometry's 39 in 769 s, the export's and morphoview's 36 in 229 s, on four CPUs shared with the mutant runs).\n\n## Not done\n\n- The export on a real mask. That is grid work on the owner's count, after SchwingNet re-vendors the merged commit with `morphoview/lines.py` and passes `--lines` (the handoff lists the steps).\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nFour reviewers read 4086684 by correctness, robustness on the grid, fitness for PR 45's stage 1, and the tests and the words; two skeptics tried the first finding and could not refute it (both reproduced it). The skeptics of the other findings were stopped to save the session's plan, and each fix is held instead by a test that fails without it.\n\n- **Confirmed, fixed: three of the seven chords had no line** (h_post, canal_w, canal_ap), though PR 45's minimal shape model is fitted on all seven. `morphoview.lines` draws them, and a test holds every one of `scanimport.SEVEN` drawn at every level.\n- **Fixed: the words promised a line for every measure;** only 22 of a lumbar vertebra's 81 keys had one. The words now name the 25 and 3 keys that have one, and a test holds the keys drawn to `VERTEBRA_KEYS` and `DISC_KEYS`.\n- **Fixed: the geometry was written to four places,** so a frame read back was orthonormal only to 1e-4 and failed the oracle interface's check at 1e-6. It is written whole.\n- **Fixed: the ends were unnamed,** their order set builder by builder, three chords opposite to specs' order. Each end is named.\n- **Fixed: frames.csv did not say which axis its z lies along,** or the column's line it was turned from. It does.\n- **Fixed: the frame tests passed with wrong frames** (the origin at zero, x and y reversed, 5 degrees off, left on the column's line). Frames tests them on the leaning chain.\n- **Fixed: one failing builder dropped every line of its level.** Each builder has its own guard.\n- **Fixed: on a vertebra the volume's edge cuts, the reused pedicle reading was not the same as reading again** (it dropped a chord line). Such a vertebra's sides are read again, and SameLines holds the cut L4.\n- **Fixed: after a run a dead worker cut short, the joins mixed studies an older code wrote with the run's.** They take only the studies of the run's stamp, written whole.\n- **Fixed: no test held the write order or the reset of what was kept after a failed measuring.** Failing kills a study at each of its writes and fails one after its vertebrae are kept.\n- **Fixed: the cost was \"about 5 per cent\";** measured on three columns it is 9 to 13.\n- **Fixed, from the review of the tests and the words: no test held a value against its measured,** a line off its row keeping both values, the stamp following the drawing's code, or a further segment's own ends. Each has a test now. The timing and the phantoms' wording are corrected (five sixths, 3.5 of 4.2 s; SameLines measures in memory), and the end-name test reads every pair either way round.\n\nLeft, with the reason, in the handoff:\n\n- **A run whose pool breaks still exits 0,** as every run has, with the lines or without, and prints \"a worker died ... run again\". SchwingNet's report is to read that line from the run's log, rather than the engine changing what its callers rely on.\n- **A key with no line leaves no line row** (\"no line\" rows were the other fix offered); `VERTEBRA_KEYS` and `DISC_KEYS` give the denominator.\n- **The oracle's and the mask-free frames PR 45's stage 1 compares** need the CT and autoanatomist, which the job has not; they are a step of their own.\n- **SchwingNet's pinned copy has no morphoview and its job passes no `--lines`.** That is SchwingNet's change, in its own pull request, before the counted jobs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Pn5qEJbGG6tvpFq8R3s7FA\n"
